WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.240
There was a point when.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.679
You know, I stood in my closet

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.149
holding a 45 caliber pistol.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.679
And I didn't want to go back to

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.729
that.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.589
Scott Mann is a Green Beret and a

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.479
military veteran who suffered

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.549
from severe trauma after

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.550
he returned from

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.539
Afghanistan.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.459
He resolved never to go back to

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.559
that part of the world again.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.449
It was a pretty dark transition, a

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.159
lot of survivor's guilt, a lot of

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.749
challenges with purpose coming out

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.089
of, you know, multiple combat tours

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.949
and really got to a place

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.779
in my life where I saw where things

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.279
were going in Afghanistan.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.749
I saw where things were going with

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.579
with a very careerist military.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.449
And I just didn't want to be a part

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.450
of it anymore.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.869
The Taliban is in control

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.999
of Afghanistan and Western countries

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.279
are scrambling to get people out.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.019
Thousands of people continue to try

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.879
and get into the airport and onto

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.899
a flight.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.369
But as the Americans acknowledged,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.139
while they control the airport, they

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.879
no longer control the entire

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.469
process.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.599
In August of 2021, he received

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.639
a call from Afghan special operator

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.659
Nizam.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.279
It was very obvious that he was in

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:09.089
severe duress.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.499
He had been shot through the face,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.839
defending a US team from an ambush.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.459
Like this guy was, you know, the

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.559
quintessential special operator

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.149
and truly a brother.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.039
And when he called me, he said

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.789
to me, "Sir, I'm not afraid to die.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.729
I just don't want to die alone." And

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.649
it just that just brought me to my

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.539
core that we can that, you

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.639
know, how do I leave this guy?

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.809
How do we leave this guy?

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:32.939
I ended up calling a couple of

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.009
buddies who were still on active

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.959
duty, who had fought with Nezam,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.429
who loved him dearly.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.409
And they were like, hell yeah,

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.789
let's do it. Let's, you know, let's

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.679
get him out. And and then

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.479
I called a congressman.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.859
That was also that's also a Green

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.779
Beret and a couple other

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.639
folks. And

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.439
we started putting a plan together.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.449
We moved him through the city

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.489
in a dingy old taxicab, and his

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.409
phone was like on 10% power.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.419
And, you know, we're thinking we're

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.439
going to lose him.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.389
He is wanted by the Taliban and

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.499
he's going to be, you know, swinging

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.659
by a lamppost by nightfall.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.490
So we had one last

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:12.359
play, and it was an email

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.249
and a phone number to a diplomat on

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.079
the inside named JP that

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.549
we had been given.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.559
So out of desperation, Hail Mary,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.509
we called that number and in just

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.739
a couple of minutes explained the

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.599
story of Nezam, how he had

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.429
taken a bullet through the face.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.409
He paused and he said,

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.789
"You know, I was a Green Beret

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.649
before I was a diplomat."

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.849
And he goes, "Tell him to say

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.189
pineapple." So we're like screaming

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.959
pineapple into the phone, you know?

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.819
And a few minutes later,

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.409
we get a selfie of Nezam on the

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.579
other side of the wire.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.690
And he had been pulled through.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.699
Then my phone just started blowing

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.589
up and it

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:50.419
was from, you

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.420
know, old friends.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.179
That we're going through the same

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.419
thing.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.420
You know.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.489
And I looked at my wife and I was

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.490
like, well,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.189
you know, what are we going to do

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.299
here? And she's like, You know what

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.649
you have to do.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.779
So that is how Task Force Pineapple

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:13.979
began.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.149
Mann received The Reason

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.009
Foundation's 2022

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.139
Sarvis Award for Privatization,

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.329
which recognizes his extraordinary

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:22.979
effort in creating a volunteer

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.959
network that saved hundreds

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.909
of Afghan nationals after

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.889
the U.S. withdrawal.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.419
When the U.S. hastily announced a

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.369
departure date from the country, it

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.109
wasn't clear what would happen to

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.729
the thousands of Afghans who had

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.259
worked directly with military

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.359
personnel during the war and thus

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.819
faced retribution from the Taliban.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.619
I've done enough interviews on this

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.479
that I'm convinced there was not

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.459
a concrete plan.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.349
And when I ask about a plan to the

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.909
to the men and women who were really

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.799
at the NCO level and the company

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:53.759
commander level, they just start

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.669
laughing.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.639
You know, there was not a plan for

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.199
the evacuation.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.969
Man and his team developed a system

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.439
for helping those who had worked

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.329
with U.S. forces to navigate

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.339
their way to Abbey Gate, the main

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.019
security checkpoint at the Kabul

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:07.859
airport.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.329
Then they recruited military

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.099
personnel known as conductors to

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.959
pick them out from the crowd.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.722
And they would look for a green chem

00:04:14.723 --> 00:04:16.739
light from the conductor

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.389
when they saw the green chem light.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.949
They would hold up a symbol of the

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.569
pineapple on their phone.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.579
And then the conductor, who

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.559
had a baseball card with picture and

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.999
numbering party, would call out

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.529
their name, would ask for their name

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.389
and number in the party.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.129
If it was correct, they would pull

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.659
their party and count them out, put

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.919
them in highlight's trucks and drive

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:35.909
them across the airfield for

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:36.929
processing.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.119
And so that became our

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:39.989
underground railroad.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.879
And we put it in full swing for

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.799
about a 72 hour period

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.659
to move hundreds of Afghans

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.129
through the wire.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.929
Scott continues to advocate for the

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.669
thousands of Afghans who worked with

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.529
U.S. forces but are still in

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.389
hiding within the country with

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.859
no escape plan.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.929
We had 6000 people

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.879
on our manifest who were in safe

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.739
houses. We had 20

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.169
kids born in safe houses

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.059
post explosion.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.469
One of the things I'm probably, I

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.509
guess, most proud

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.399
of is that we were

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.409
able to raise enough

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.329
revenue to keep our

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.089
6000 person manifest

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.090
to get them through the winter.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.899
And some of them didn't make it.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.219
Some of them were assassinated,

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.059
hunted, and killed.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.219
And there are hundreds

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.409
of veterans, not just in Pineapple,

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:29.849
but in a lot of these other groups

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.559
as well. They are in a moral

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.359
quandary where they are literally

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.399
the singular lifeline to these

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.959
families, to these partners who have

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.129
no other recourse.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.049
They don't know how they can move on

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.179
with their lives, you

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.769
know, and that's a real, real

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:44.849
problem that's going to have to be

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:45.850
addressed.

